abstract: >-
  MATLAB function, which also runs in GNU Octave, solving the Serre–Green–Naghdi equations of fully nonlinear, weakly
  dispersive long gravity waves over a flat bottom on a periodic interval, with the head-on collision of two solitary
  waves as an example. The fields are expanded in Fourier series; the linear waves are propagated exactly and the
  nonlinear terms are advanced, with a constant step, by the fourth-order formula of a six-stage Runge–Kutta pair of
  Dormand and Prince, the velocity being recovered from the conserved variable by a fixed-point iteration.
